The implementation splits cleanly into three independent pieces, so I’m running them in parallel inside the permitted file patterns:

- a native pullback comparison built from `sectionsMap` and the piece trivializations;
- affine-target and basis-locality lemmas for module morphisms;
- the canonical-mate section formula needed to identify the H0 equivalence with the actual `canonicalBaseChangeMap`.

Each piece gets its own new file to avoid overlap; I’ll only integrate results that elaborate, kernel-check, and remain free of conditional `IsIso` assumptions.
